  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Friday)\nIssued at 1116 AM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nAs of 11 AM, a cold front has almost cleared the region with\nAberdeen, MS still prevailing a southerly wind and 80 degree\ndewpoint. Elsewhere, strong subsidence is occurring with\ntemperatures in the upper 70s and low 80s with brisk northerly\nflow. Temperatures should not warm too far from these current\ntemperatures due to strong mixing and post frontal stratus\ncontinuing to move in from the NW. North Mississippi may squeak\nout slightly above 90 degrees, but the front is moving very\nquickly and should clear the Mid-South by 1 PM.\n\nBehind this boundary, unseasonably cool and mostly dry conditions\nwill prevail through midweek. A normal high temperature for the\nfirst week of August is near to slightly above 90 degrees, which\ncurrently is not a forecasted high until at least Tuesday. NBM\ndoes have a cool bias with very dry airmasses, but with dewpoint\nvalues in the 60s, it will certainly feel significantly cool for\nthis time of year. A few stray showers could develop along the\nTennessee River Valley as the trough continues to pull away, but\nconfidence is low in accumulation values. Perhaps a few sprinkles\nup to a tenth of an inch, but the dry air aloft will prohibit\ndownpours.\n\nAfter Tuesday, upper level ridging will emerge near the Baja of\nCalifornia and slowly traverse east. A few shortwaves may spew\nout ahead, with low end diurnally driven PoPs added to the\nforecast. QPF is very uncertain due to the intensity and\nlongevity of the dry air aloft, but showers and thunderstorms\ncannot be ruled out in the embedded waves. The ridge will heat\nthings back up gradually from Wednesday through the end of the\nwork week. By Friday, medium chance probabilities return to the\nDelta region for heat index values meeting or exceeding 105F\n(Heat Advisory criteria). Those probabilities begin to expand\ngeographically north and eastward for the remainder of the next\nweekend. Until then, enjoy the cooler temperatures!\n\nDNM",
